# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of the checkout platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into e2e/docker/*.sh, Docker COPYs
# the file verbatim, and the container fails at the shebang with:
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# — i.e. the real-CLI e2e gate becomes unrunnable on the platform this project is developed on.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else consumed by a Linux container or a POSIX shell.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
